  'sakai-knife-maker-or-blacksmith-walking-tour-in-osaka': {
            averageRating: 4.79,
            totalReviews: 89,
            guideRating: 4.91,
            valueRating: 4.56,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Karen", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-09-17", text: "Remi was lovely and the Sakai knife makers skills where nicely shown. Brilliant walking tour for those interested in Kitchen / professional level knives for cooking or just learning something new." },
                { author: "Oscar", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-23", text: "Our tour guide Remmi was incredibly knowledgeable. We learned so much from not only Sakai knife district but Japanese culture and traditions." },
                { author: "Pavel", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-07", text: "The guide was very helpful.. and even though it was raining it was worth it. thanks" },
                { author: "Gail", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-05", text: "Jean Yves was a great tour guide. Very knowledgeable, professional and personable. We enjoyed the all the places visited and it was special to watch Eric the blacksmith go through the various processes of knife making. Highly recommend." },
                { author: "Miguel", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-19", text: "Scott was a fantastic guide, sharing history and stories about Sakai and why its famous knives are masterpieces. The stellar moment was when Erick, the master blacksmith let us forge a piece of steel." },
                { author: "Justin", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-01-15", text: "The tour was great. We walked through the Sakai district and visited an old original mochi maker / shop. Our guide Remy was very engaging and knowledgeable about the history of the area and associated stories. The knife museum was interesting and worthwhile seeing. The highlight was the visit to the blacksmith Eric who has his own small old style workshop. Seeing him work and talk through the steps of knife making was great. The highlight was definitely being given a go at hammering down the glowing steel as the starting point to making a knife. Would definitely recommend! Thanks" },
                { author: "Alice", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-12-08", text: "I picked this tour for my husband because he loves knives. I knew he would get a lot out of it. Scott was our guide. He knew the ins and outs of the area and the local purveyors. I liked the mix of history of the area on the Portuguese “discovery” to the local vibe of going to a very old mochi shop where we tried their signature poppyseed mochi and cinnamon mochi. We also checked out the museum. The key is to go on Wednesdays because that is the only day where you visit the Knife Maker, Eric Chevallier. This was one of our highlights of the trip, learning and trying out how to hand forge! He i" },
                { author: "Nahrin", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-11-09", text: "I did the blacksmith walking tour and had Scott for the guide. Scott was great, really nice and friendly and knows how to get a group of strangers engaged. The tour is very interesting and has more to it than just visiting the blacksmith. We learnt about Sakai local history, visiting a traditional sweets shop and met with that owner. Then we went to meet the blacksmith Eric Chevalier, we got to see him at work, got a bit involved, learned a lot about blacksmithing. It was a really good and interesting day. Highly recommend it." },
                { author: "Barbara", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-10-31", text: "An excellent mixture of exploring the surroundings and learning something about the history of Japan and Sakai. The visit at the Mocchi shop was the highlight before we turned to the reason of our booking: knives. A short visit at the knives museum before we actually visited the factory. It was amazing to be able to peek over the masters shoulders while doing different steps in the knife production process. I also appreciated the hands-on-experience for knife sharpening. I'm confident I can handle it at home now. Our guide also perfectly supervised and translated our knife shopping. The final" },
                { author: "Marius", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-10-24", text: "The tour with Scott was very informative and entertaining. All topics were very exciting. Due to two simultaneous tours and a subsequent chaos, I only wanted to give a 4 star rating. However, the J.T.A. Team really every effort to offer the best possible experience. I noticed that when I was contacted after an accidental one star rating. So thumbs up! 5 stars and a clear recommendation ;)" },
                { author: "Christian", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-10-16", text: "The tour was amazing, one of the best I took in 2 month traveling Japan. To learn about the different crafts present in Sakai and experiencing them was amazing. Thank you for the tour." },
                { author: "S.", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-07-24", text: "The tour was great, the guide Jean-Yves explained everything with great enthusiasm and knowledge. It was fun, educational and a perfect way to look into the kitchen of a knife making industry. Thanks a lot!" }
            ]
        },
