  'samurai-sword-class-by-experts-in-traditional-arts-in-kyoto': {
            averageRating: 4.85,
            totalReviews: 841,
            guideRating: 4.85,
            valueRating: 4.76,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Hannah", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-09-16", text: "I am a solo traveler and i had so much fun. There was a couple of groups but the organizers made sure I was able to get photos and videos. It was fun meeting new people too" },
                { author: "Emil", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-09-12", text: "Very happy with this experience. There were 2 parts to it: 3 masters performing kenbu theatre based on samurai poetry, which was intense, obviously involving swords and certain themes around life and death of a samurai. The second part was us being instructed by Julia, our guide on the day, on the basic sword moves, dressing up as samurai and performing on stage. This was for the long/full experience, which I highly recommend. The short experience has the same kenbu theatre but very little practice time afterwards." },
                { author: "Amy", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-09-07", text: "This was a highlight of our trip. The show was spectacular, very kind and wonderful staff. Myself and my partner ended up being very lucky to be the only two booked in for the lesson and it was AMAZING! The outfits, the choreography and patience from Kika was brilliant. Lots of videos and photos and lovely keepsakes from the experience too. Thank you so much!!! It was amazing!!" },
                { author: "Amanda", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-22", text: "We had a fantastic time! It was so much fun getting to pick out what to wear, and learning the steps using the samurai sword. We also loved getting to do the performance at the end! I highly recommend this activity we had a blast and it was one of the highlights of our trip!" },
                { author: "Marcus", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-19", text: "Was a super cool experience! Fun and professional at the same time" },
                { author: "Patrick", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-18", text: "This was one of our highlights for sure! Loved learning the routine, and wearing the traditional outfit with sword was amazing!" },
                { author: "Mohamed", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-14", text: "Very good , thanks you Julia Sensei , Arigatō Gozaimasu 🙏" },
                { author: "Mitchell", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-03", text: "Very enjoyable experience learning about the art of kenbu!" },
                { author: "Barbara", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-29", text: "The class started with the fitting of a samurai suit. The staff was very attentive and helped with getting dressed in the traditional garments. After that we started the class and learned how to draw the sword, and different forms of attacks and how to holster the sword again. We learned the movements with the fan and even practiced a small choreography. After our class was over our sensei Hisyo took pictures in different poses for us. The Kenbu show at the end of the class was very impressive and enjoyable to watch. As as side note: as a bigger person I had issues in the past with these fitti" },
                { author: "Chris", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-28", text: "As a family we were so impressed how inclusive the session was. The instructors were excellent. They were friendly, fun and patient. I would highly recommend this for families. We were in a group of ten some together and others alone but the session was aimed at inclusivity and teamwork. We learnt so much about the culture and history of the Samurai." },
                { author: "Barbara", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-15", text: "This was a very enjoyable experience overall. It was interactive and felt like actual samurai training, which made it both fun and memorable. My only suggestions would be to slow down the pace a little and reduce the group size, as there were many participants and it sometimes felt rushed. I also wish there had been more costume options available. That said, I had a great time and would recommend it to anyone looking for a unique cultural experience. For younger children under 10, it may be a bit less suitable." },
                { author: "Monica", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-06-23", text: "This was a A+ family friendly experience! We got to dress in costumes and learn traditional sword and fan dances. Our teacher was very knowledgeable, funny, and assisted with pictures for our family." }
            ]
        },
