                { author: "Robert", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-14", text: "Wow!! We had a wonderful time! Our tour leader, Marielle, was a warm, welcoming and brilliant guide. She is also a middle school teacher, so her ability to impart knowledge was first class. The meeting point was easy to find and after a short walk though the back streets we arrived at the Temple, then down to nearby boat wharf for picturesque cruise along the river to a historic loch gate where we got off the boat at a small museum about the engineering history of Kyoto’s waterways. After returning to the wharf it was on to the historic Sake distillery for an enjoyable tasting with 9 options t" },
                { author: "Howard", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-11-04", text: "Very good guide , who was very good at giving an overall history of Kyoto not just the sake industry." },
                { author: "Daria", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-09-24", text: "A magical tour that gives an insight into traditional and modern sake making. We tasted several types of sake at the museum, housed in a historic building, and bought a bottle of the most delicious one to take home. After tasting, it was a delightful short boat ride from the nearby boat station. It was a wonderful way to start the day, inspiring you to explore Kyoto with renewed vigor! Highly recommended!" }
