                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-12-30", text: "They offers an exceptional yakiniku experience in a space infused with the refined aesthetic of Kyoto. The moment you step through the entrance, you are greeted by an elegant atmosphere reminiscent of a traditional Kyoto townhouse, instantly transporting you away from the ordinary. Soft, ambient lighting fills the interior, creating a calm and sophisticated setting that feels more like a traditional ryotei than a typical yakiniku restaurant. It is an ideal place for special occasions or a memorable meal with someone important. For this visit, we chose a Premium Yasaka Kaiseki course and a few" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-12-30", text: "This yakiniku restaurant is tucked away in a quiet corner of Gion, about a 10-minute walk from Keihan Gion-Shijo Station. From the moment you step inside, the atmosphere is wonderful—it truly captures the essence of Kyoto. Each cut of the main yakiniku dishes was thoughtfully prepared, either pre-seasoned or meant to be grilled with carefully selected condiments. This is yakiniku at its finest in Japan. Everything was absolutely delicious—I lost count of how many times I said “this is amazing.” We also ordered chateaubriand off the course menu. It was served as a whole block, and because of it" }
