  'day-trip-to-amanohashidate-and-ine-from-osaka-kyoto-by-local-operator': {
            averageRating: 4.09,
            totalReviews: 25,
            guideRating: 3.27,
            valueRating: 4.1,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Cynthia", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-22", text: "Amazing Job! We were very impressed by the views and Lui was a great guide in letting us know the history and where to go when we got off the bus. He was very accommodating with the different types of things people booked (food, cable car, boat etc) and translating for all the guests too. He also messaged everyone maps and timing of when we should be back at the bus which was very helpful." },
                { author: "Shelton", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-08", text: "The trip is wonderful, and the guides are very organized and professional." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 1, date: "2026-09-01", text: "In Japan I experienced so far from mediocre to very good guides, but Mingjie He was the worst. His English was barely understandable in the bus and he took much care for the Chinese travellers. First, the tour started delayed and this time was taken off from the visiting time at the first stop where we spent some time on the beach. my daughter and myself came 1 minute late before planned departure, but the others of our group were 5 minutes behind but MingjieHe let the bus depart without us. so we were separated from my non adolscent daughter. then he wrote a Whatsapp that we could take a publ" },
                { author: "Christy", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-13", text: "there was plenty of free time to enjoy the area" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 3, date: "2026-07-30", text: "We were expecting much more from the trip and while our guide had to translate the information into three languages, we tended to feel lost and left to figure things out for ourselves" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 3, date: "2026-07-22", text: "The guide barely spoke English and mostly repeated phrases 10 times every time. He spoke to us only on the bus and gave us return times for every activity. I frankly felt guided like I was a prisoner and some activities were pretty much meaningless (45 mins in a fishermen village, where the only open place was an information office..?). Plus, out of the 11 hours, 6 were transportation.. Bottomline, a truly bad experience" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 3, date: "2026-07-04", text: "Timing serré et pression temporelle imposée par le guide. Guide parlant un Anglais difficile à comprendre et parlant principalement Chinois…. Trop touristique…." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-06-30", text: "Endroits magnifiques ! Un peu plus de temps (15-20mn de plus ) aurait été bien pour visiter la maison des pêcheurs dans le dernier village et les petits achats souvenirs ou boissons…" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-12", text: "Jay war ein sehr guter Guide und war top organisiert. Er hat uns lustige Hintergründe mitgeteilt. Wir haben 2,5h freie Zeit in Amanoshidate und nochmal 0,45h freie Zeit in Ine bekommen. Amanohashidate ist ein wunderschöner Ort, vor allem wenn man die Seilbahn hochfährt. Das gute Wetter hat natürlich auch geholfen. In Ine gab es eine Bootsfahrt, von wo aus man die Möwen füttern konnte. Oder die traumhafte Landschaft genießen mit den Holzbauten am Ufer. Wirklich empfehlenswert :)" },
                { author: "John", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 3, date: "2026-02-27", text: "For an excursion that took that long, there was not a whole lot to do. Although, Amanohashidate was a nice place, the top of the mountain was completely outdated. Not a lot for adults to do or places to eat. The chairlift was fun. Ine fishing village was a very nice place to visit. I am sure it’s even better during the warmer season. I was able to take great pictures from both locations. The guide was a little awkward though. He tried with his jokes and he could’ve done better with his speeches. Nevertheless, it’s a good tour for the price. I would recommend it for those visiting Kyoto or Osak" }
            ]
        },
