  'kyoto-natural-indigo-dyeing-with-local-masters-by-local-operator': {
            averageRating: 5.0,
            totalReviews: 43,
            guideRating: 5.0,
            valueRating: 4.89,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Rebecca", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-09-15", text: "Three of us, all experienced dyers, booked back to back classes. The studio arranged for us to do 4 hours all at once. We all did different techniques and had lots of fun learning their way of doing indigo." },
                { author: "Robert", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-06-14", text: "So glad I found this opportunity to participate in an authentic indigo dyeing class outside the touristy areas of Kyoto. I recommend taking a taxi to/from the atelier, would be quite difficult trying to navigate with buses. Overall a great experience where I got to learn about history of indigo in Japan, dye my own piece, and even get invited to have indigo tea with the owners. The guide was so kind and spoke English perfectly. Would recommend for those looking for something different & unique." },
                { author: "Kara", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-06-09", text: "From the very start of our workshop the team here made us feel welcome and took the time to answer our questions and ensure we had the best experience as well as benefiting from their knowledge and skills. Both the assistants and the owner took part in the workshop and it was wonderful to see a true artisanal setup. Can’t recommend it enough for those interested in the arts and heritage crafts." },
                { author: "Shelby", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-28", text: "This was an amazing experience! The staff are incredibly knowledgeable and kind. They walked us through the farm to dye vat journey the indigo had been on and helped us select beautiful patterns for our pieces. We were even able to add an extra piece to the dye vat for just a bit extra because we had trouble narrowing down our choices. They have a number of dye patterns they can show you how to achieve and you can always freestyle. I would definitely do this workshop again. This was our high point in our trip to kyoto!" },
                { author: "Kelly", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-22", text: "We had a wonderful time learning about the authenticity of indigo dyeing. Everyone was so helpful and informative during the experience. Would highly recommend this workshop." },
                { author: "Julie", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-13", text: "This was a fun and interesting activity. The guides were so friendly and helpful and spoke excellent English. Would highly recommend." },
                { author: "mbn", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-01", text: "I had the very best time ! The place was really intimate and the persons that work here are genuinely happy to share their passion for indigo dyeing. Some of them being in the field for more than 15years ! They let you choose your pattern, show you how to make it and leave the rest to you while checking everything goes smoothly just aside you. I would 100% recommend trying this very traditional 400y.o piece of Japanese history" },
                { author: "Danielle", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-21", text: "This was easily the best experience of our trip! From getting to learn about the history of the art from the Indigo Master, to the hands-on experience of dyeing, to sharing stories and chatting with the shop owner over tea, and to receiving our final projects, I cannot recommend this experience enough. I would do it again in a heartbeat!" },
                { author: "Gil", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-21", text: "We had an amazing experience. The team’s warm hospitality, professionalism, and detailed explanations created a truly memorable workshop. Although textile dyeing is not my hobby (it is my wife’s hobby), I still found the workshop very interesting, and we both had a great time. Thank you very much, Chie, Skye, and the Indigo dye team." },
                { author: "Eleanor", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-07", text: "A fabulous experience! A highlight of my trip to Japan. The staff were so friendly and helpful. Hands on experience of natural indigo dying. I was so very happy with my end product. I recommend highly." },
                { author: "Maria", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-06", text: "This was a highlight of our time in Kyoto. What a fun and crafty learning experience . Everyone was so helpful and patient. We all enjoyed making our pieces and learning about how indigo is grown, processed and used in doing. Thank you for a unique experience . !" },
                { author: "Susan", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-24", text: "amazing. simply amazing. being able to learn from masters of dyeing and so very friendly. the translation was excellent and we had so much fun learning about the process of natural indigo dyeing. if you are curious about it at all, I highly recommend doing this tour, you will not regret it!" }
            ]
        },
