                { author: "Acey", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-23", text: "Thanks to a cancellation, I had Hiro all to myself. By the end of the tour, it felt more like I was hanging out with a friend than being shown the sights by a guide." },
                { author: "Eleonora", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-15", text: "We can't express enough how much we loved this tour. It was informative, fun and our tour guide, Masa-San was exceptional with his knowledge. He was fun and a very very good guide with good recommendations for Kyoto and Osaka" },
                { author: "Jonathan", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-17", text: "Our tour guide Teppei was hilarious, polite and Informative. We really enjoyed our afternoon and visiting the 3 Sake breweries. Although the 18 Sake tasting at the Fushimi Sake Village would have been more than enough for our crew. Arigatou gozaimasu Teppei!" },
                { author: "MTS", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-12", text: "Satoshi was an excellent guide and was very knowledgeable about sake and the region" },
                { author: "Cameron", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-07", text: "Julien was amazing, tour was very interesting would really recommend! Must do in Kyoto" },
                { author: "Rachael", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-16", text: "Julien was absolutely fantastic! We learned so much about sake history, which was quite fascinating. Our experience would have been lacking had we toured the breweries in our own. Be prepared to drink a lot of sake and truly appreciate the science and history behind sake making. Thanks again Julien!" },
                { author: "Bartłomiej", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-12-18", text: "Together with my partner we selected private sake tasting for a little extra charge and I must say it was worth it! Mr Yoshi our guide was punctual, very professional, knowledgable about the process of making sake, as well as history of Japan - adding few historical facts made this tour very immersive, allowing us to appreciate Japanese culture even more. This tour was entertaining and educational - taught us about differences between sake types which allowed us to choose the perfect gifts for our friends and family. Mr Yoshi's professionalism is truly outstanding, his approach was very respec" }
