  'sake-tasting-tour-at-the-birthplace-of-japanese-sake-in-nara': {
            averageRating: 4.97,
            totalReviews: 18,
            guideRating: 5.0,
            valueRating: 4.71,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Jess", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-06-01", text: "The guide was very knowledgeable and even had paper handouts with info about sake on them. The sake itself was delicious and the places he brought me to were great. I even had the chance to befriend a deer." },
                { author: "Eva", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-26", text: "Our guide Eri was knowledgeable and very nice, she taught us a lot about sake, considered our individual preferences and even gave us recommendations for Kyoto! We absolutely adored the tour with her. Only the price could be a bit less, as the Sake Tastings themselves at the breweries were considerably cheaper than booking the tour here. 10/10 for Eri though!" },
                { author: "Carly", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-24", text: "Literally the best tour we did on our trip to Japan! We have tried Sake before and done a few tasting sessions but Takashi & Juliette knew so much more than we'd been told and were awesome guides. We even managed to stop off at a local historical open house in-between tasting sessions that used to house nobility. We stopped at three breweries and got to try and very large variety of sake! All of which seemed very good quality. Then stopped off at a local bar for more sake and got to try sake lees soup which is a must! The location of the tour is picturesque and we also passed a lot of shrines" },
                { author: "Tima", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-23", text: "Amazing experience in Nara. We visited local spots we never would’ve found on our own, which made it feel really authentic. Yoshi was an excellent guide, knowledgeable and fun, and made the whole experience even better. Definitely worth it and highly recommend if you want something unique." },
                { author: "Vladislav", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-22", text: "Yoshiki went above and beyond when guiding us around Nara. He met us near the Nara park, showed us around three different sake breweries and an izakaya. He was very knowledgeable about Nara and Japan history and shared a lot of interesting facts about the region and the country. Yoshiki also recommended us a great ramen place in Umeda and even took us there. He also recommended a tour around Kyoto because we might be missing out on a few places, which I’d love to do but I managed to get sick just before it 😢 Six stars out of five!" },
                { author: "Denise", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-31", text: "Satoshi provided a very informative tour into the history and making of Sake. We got to experience 3 breweries which were all a little different so provided for an interesting mix. We also got to learn a little history about Nara along the way & explored some traditional preserved local residential areas which we otherwise would not have found. Very professional service from Satoshi. We were very satisfied with the experience and highly recommend" },
                { author: "Jade", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-25", text: "Wasn’t sure what to expect, but the tour was fantastic. We were taken to local sake brewery’s and bars that you would not necessarily find unless you were local. I was really happy with the sake taste offering, we received mostly full glasses for tasting (sake cup size). The final stop we had an option for some small food which we opted for over the tasting only. Eri, who was our guide was very knowledgeable and fun. She took many photos for us and taught us all about sake in this region. I recommend the tour and feel it was good value for money. My only suggestion is to offer group tours in a" },
                { author: "Cesar", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-19", text: "Excellent experience and our guide was wonderful! Looking forward to doing it again in the future!" },
                { author: "Kyle", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-01-28", text: "Hiro Takeuchi made this a wonderful experience. He was very personable, friendly and courteous. He was very gracious accommodating my Father in a wheelchair. We had an amazing time trying some delicious types of Sake native to Nara. It was a remarkable experience and definitely one to remember. I highly recommend this tour to get a feel for the neighborhoods in Nara as well as the local shopkeepers. 10/10 Will do again." },
                { author: "Karyl", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-11-02", text: "What a fantastic way to spend the afternoon! Our guide was wonderful, so funny, so knowledgeable and so kind. Takashi was one of the best guides we have ever had in Japan. We went to some great sake places, enjoyed every minute. If you want personalised service with a smile, you can't go wrong with this tour, truly wonderful! Thanks Takashi ☺️" },
                { author: "Jesper", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-10-29", text: "This was truly an amazing experience. We got to experience the history and taste of sake with an amazing guide. I highly recommend that you experience this if you are ever in Nara" },
                { author: "Jacqui", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-10-02", text: "Thank you so much Takashi! What a beautiful afternoon 💖 We appreciated his knowledge, hospitality, and generosity in sharing Nara and the gift of sake! Takashi took us to a great range of breweries, added some extra activities along the way- he even helped us shop for items we hadn’t been able to find yet. We felt very blessed to be with him for a whole afternoon." }
            ]
        },
