  'urban-canvas-osaka-street-art-bike-tour-by-local-operator': {
            averageRating: 5.0,
            totalReviews: 20,
            guideRating: 5.0,
            valueRating: 4.86,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Kristin", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-09-05", text: "Thanks Eric. The tour was fantastic. We really appreciated that you knew most of the artists as well as being one of them yourself. The murals were all very different and interesting. The bikes were in good condition. I really enjoyed visiting the old Japanese store/bar. The tour covered many different scenes from green, river, busy streets and shops. Would definitely recommend. Lisa" },
                { author: "Lisa", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-17", text: "This is a must if you are visiting Osaka. Eric was such a gracious host - it didn’t even feel like a tour. Not only did we get to see fantastic murals, we also got to experience true Osaka - from a hip coffee house, a dive snack bar (go Dodgers!) and finally some of the best pizza we’ve ever had at Hughes Pizza. Such a great way to spend a day with our new friend…and learn all about the artists. (the bikes were great too!)" },
                { author: "Marjo", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-02", text: "Great bike and great tour. It is a nice way to see the street art and the real Osaka life. Joel was a very good guide, a lot of good info and helpful on all questions. Good food and drink as well." },
                { author: "Michael", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-10-19", text: "Amazing urban art work, Eric was a fantastic guide who has a passion for the art displays and great knowledge of the works." },
                { author: "Milly", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-05-16", text: "Fantastic! A great way to see an ‘off-the-beaten-track’ view of Osaka. The art was incredible and Eric was very knowledgeable. We loved the little snacks stood along the way too - all wonderful places. Great day out. The only thing I would say is I would have loved a little pamphlet at the end with the info Eric told us about the different artworks - I can never remember the interesting facts later! Haha." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-16", text: "Unique experience and best guide, definitely worth trying." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-13", text: "Die Tour hat richtig Spaß gemacht. Es war schön das Osaka der Locals zu sehen und nicht nur die Hotpots." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-28", text: "Fantastisch! Ruben wist op een hele leuke en toegankelijke manier te vertellen over alle kunstwerken. En vertelde ook veel over Osaka. Super leuk ook de afwerking met de koffie, de mochi en de pizza punten! Een aanrader!" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-11", text: "Extraordinary journey to discover some decidedly little-known neighborhoods of Osaka and especially street art. Thanks to Joel artist photographer wonderful guide !" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-01-23", text: "the tour was fantastic, awesome guide and the street art is like nothing I've seen before, zipping around the streets of osaka on a bike was a blast too!" },
                { author: "Barbara", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-11-07", text: "Wir waren zu dritt unterwegs. Unser guide Ruben hat sich für uns Zeit genommen alle Fragen zu streetart, aber auch zu Osaka und Japan zu beantworten. Es blieb genügend Zeit alle Werke zu fotografieren und in einem guten Tempo sicher die 23 km zu radeln. Die Tour gibt einen prima Einblick in ein anderes Osaka - fernab des Trubels, Leuchtreklame und Hochhäusern. Kleine Pausen mit Kaffee; ineiner Bar und Pizzeria waren eine gute Stärkung auf der fast 4h Tour. Vielen Dank Ruben für die bunte Streetart-Zeit!" }
            ]
        },
