  'osaka-private-custom-tour-with-local-guide-by-local-operator': {
            averageRating: 4.47,
            totalReviews: 13,
            guideRating: 4.33,
            valueRating: 3.33,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Peter", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-02-02", text: "Osaka Castle. Our guide Kosuke was excellent. He knew all the history." },
                { author: "Larry", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-10-28", text: "Kosuke did a great job, we don't walk fast so he took his time and made sure we didn't miss anything. Learned somethings about the subways which will be helpful. Good value, highly recommend Larry & Janet" },
                { author: "Heather", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-10-12", text: "Our guide, Kosuke , worked with us to plan the perfect tour. He even suggested an attraction we did not know about. He was insightful and helpful. He answered all our questions and was great to work with- HIGHLY RECOMMEND!" },
                { author: "June", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-05-17", text: "It was an amazing experience. Andy was a great guide, he knew so much and was so much fun. The food was delicious and they were very careful with my allergies. Thank you for everything" },
                { author: "Lucy", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 4, date: "2026-09-13", text: "We met our guide, Kosuke, at our hotel and took the train to our first stop, Osaka Castle (entry not included in the tour price). Kosuke was incredibly knowledgeable about the history of Japan.The castle was amazing, and despite the crowds, he managed to show us around the entire place and share lots of interesting information. We then visited a Hokoku Shrine, where Kosuke explained the etiquette when entering the shrine. It was fascinating to learn about the traditions and customs. Next, we headed to Kuromon Market for delicious and authentic Takoyaki. From there, we made our way to the bustl" },
                { author: "Judit", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 4, date: "2025-08-10", text: "The company was very accommodating with our last-minute bookings (we made three) and requests. Communication via WhatsApp was extremely quick and easy. Our tour guide in Osaka knew the city very well, was extremely patient and polite, and without rushing us even once, we managed to see all the planned spots. Kosuke guided us smoothly from one place to another and even purchased entry tickets with his app so we could skip the lines—something we greatly appreciated given the high temperatures. Our teenagers also enjoyed chatting with him. On the other hand, I would have appreciated more in-depth" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-08-17", text: "nous avons bien apprécié le guide et ses explications ainsi que sa disponibilité pour des sollicitations italiens annexes sur les transports etc..." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-02-22", text: "Super amazing guide, route, everything was perfect. I recommend this tour to anyone who is visiting Osaka." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-10-24", text: "Soma was an excellent guide, making our Osaka tour both informative and fun. He shared great stories at Osaka Castle and Dotonbori, and his knowledge of local food at Kuromon Market was impressive. Soma’s friendly and engaging personality made the tour a highlight of our trip. Highly recommend him for a memorable Osaka experience!" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-10-23", text: "The Osaka tour was a fantastic way to explore the city's highlights in a short amount of time. We started with Osaka Castle, where the rich history and stunning architecture immediately drew us in. The panoramic views from the top were breathtaking! Next, we visited Dotonbori, the lively heart of Osaka, famous for its neon lights and street food. We tasted some local favorites like takoyaki and okonomiyaki, which were absolutely delicious. Walking along the canal and seeing the iconic Glico sign was a memorable experience. The tour was well-organized, and our guide shared fascinating insights" },
                { author: "Alberto", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-10-23", text: "Soma es una persona muy amable y educada. Me gustó mucho su trato" }
            ]
        },
