  'noboribetsu-and-lake-toya-a-day-tour-sapporo': {
            averageRating: 4.8,
            totalReviews: 11,
            guideRating: 4.0,
            valueRating: 4.0,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Muhammad", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-31", text: "It is too exhausting for me to learn how to take the JR that's why I join this tour going to Lake Toya and Noboribetsu. Reaching every destination by only getting on the bus is really nice. Our tour guide, Mr. Lee told us many things about Japan and Hokkaido, including how the showa shinzan was formed. I particularly appreciate his language skills to switch between Chinese, English, Korean and Japanese. Thank you for the day." },
                { author: "ALI", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-30", text: "Noboribetsu, a.k.a hell valley is a must go place in Hokkaido. Watching smoke coming out from a barren land is simply astonishing. We visited the biggest pond in Hokkaido too." },
                { author: "Farhan", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-29", text: "The tour is well organized. Although we visited a lot of places, I do not feel tired. Thank for the the free footbath in Jozankei! Our guide, Lee, tell us that the showa shinzan formed less than 100 years ago due to a volcanic activity. His information makes our journey more fruitful." },
                { author: "Saqib", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-27", text: "Mr. Zhang is very nice and friendly that he advised me to go to the Mount Usu Ropeway. I thought that it is a bit expensive to take the Ropeway, but it is certainly worth to see the newly formed volcanic mountain at a highly level. The weather of today is a bit cloudy, otherwise it would be perfect if we can see Lake Toya with the blue sky." },
                { author: "Shahzad", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-27", text: "The tour is well arranged. We travelled to Noboribetsu, Mount Usu, Lake Toya and Jozankei. We have heard that Jozankei was just added to this tour a few days before. The free footbath here is perfect for us before the end of a wonderful day tour. Especially we need to walk quite a distance at noboribetsu." },
                { author: "Mohsin", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-27", text: "The experiences here was worth it. The timings may be just right or slightly not enough but it’s still worth the views and photo taking! But since the tour is travelling to so many place in a day, I cannot ask for more. Our guide, Zhang, gave us good recommendations and interesting information about each location that we visited." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 4, date: "2026-08-12", text: "有珠山ロープウェイ駅からの眺めがすばらしかった。教科書に記載されていた昭和新山も眺めて涙がでました。北海道らしい畑、農家、白樺林すばらしかった。ヨーロッパ都市郊外の地平線が見える平原の景色とは違うけれど、またこれはこれでとても良かったです。" }
            ]
        },
